Sources and third-party software

The page's shell (header, key handling, modals) and the LLM bridge are
adapted from Data Crawler Carl (ui-insight/data-crawler-carl) and
Promptulus (AI4RA/promptulus), both by the same authors under Apache-2.0.
The eCFR lookup is adapted from the NCURA Region VI/VII 2026 workshop site
(ui-insight/NCURARegionalWorkshop2026), Apache-2.0.

docs/index/ holds passages of 2 CFR Part 200 fetched from the eCFR
(https://www.ecfr.gov), a work of the United States Government in the
public domain, with vectors computed from them.

The site loads the following open source software in the browser from
public CDNs. Each remains under its own license and copyright; none is
modified or redistributed by this project.

Transformers.js, @huggingface/transformers 4.3.1 (sentence embeddings in the browser)
  Copyright 2023-present Hugging Face
  Apache License 2.0 - https://github.com/huggingface/transformers.js/blob/main/LICENSE
  It loads ONNX Runtime Web (MIT, Microsoft) as part of its bundle.

all-MiniLM-L6-v2, as Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2 (the embedding model, fetched
from the Hugging Face Hub at run time and at build time)
  Copyright the Sentence-Transformers authors (Nils Reimers and Iryna Gurevych)
  Apache License 2.0 - https://huggingface.co/sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2

@google/genai (Google Gen AI JavaScript SDK, loaded only when a Gemini key is used)
  Copyright 2025 Google LLC
  Apache License 2.0 - https://github.com/googleapis/js-genai/blob/main/LICENSE

The live columns call the AI4RA MCP server (ui-insight/ai4ra-mcp,
Apache-2.0), whose eCFR tools read https://www.ecfr.gov and whose web
search is a SearXNG metasearch (AGPL-3.0, run as a service, not
redistributed here).

The text of Plato's Phaedrus is quoted in Benjamin Jowett's 1892
translation, which is in the public domain.

